---
import { Picture } from 'astro:assets';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import portrait from '../assets/gallery/rivers-ne.webp';
---

<Layout title="About" description="About Ryan van der Heijden, a hydrology researcher at the University of Vermont.">
  <main class="about">
    <div class="text">
      <h1>About</h1>
      <p>
        I'm a postdoctoral associate at the University of Vermont, where I work on water resources,
        machine learning and complex systems. My research is part of the Cooperative Institute for
        Research to Operations in Hydrology (CIROH), a NOAA-funded consortium of government, academic
        and private partners working to improve national water modeling.
      </p>
      <p>
        The pictures in this gallery come out of that work. Each one is computed from real records,
        mostly USGS streamgages and gridded rainfall, and drawn as light on a black background, so
        places where many rivers or storms agree glow brighter. Color always stands for a variable.
      </p>

      <h2>Research interests</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Hydrological modeling and prediction</li>
        <li>Machine learning for environmental science</li>
        <li>Complex systems and network dynamics</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <dl>
        <dt>Email</dt><dd><a href="mailto:rvanderh@uvm.edu">rvanderh@uvm.edu</a></dd>
        <dt>GitHub</dt><dd><a href="https://github.com/Ryan-vanderHeijden">Ryan-vanderHeijden</a></dd>
        <dt>LinkedIn</dt><dd><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/ryan-van-der-heijden/">ryan-van-der-heijden</a></dd>
        <dt>Scholar</dt><dd><a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=aZ0-0SsAAAAJ&hl=en">Google Scholar</a></dd>
        <dt>ORCID</dt><dd><a href="https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1320-9500">0000-0003-1320-9500</a></dd>
      </dl>
    </div>
    <Picture
      class="side"
      src={portrait}
      alt="The stream network of New England in violet, with the main rivers glowing cyan."
      widths={[640, 1200]}
      sizes="(min-width: 960px) 45vw, 100vw"
      formats={['avif', 'webp']}
    fallbackFormat="webp"
    />
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .about {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, var(--measure)) 1fr;
    gap: 2rem clamp(2rem, 5vw, 5rem);
    padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem) var(--gutter) 0;
    align-items: start;
  }
  h1 { font-size: var(--t-h1); font-weight: 300; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  h2 { font-size: var(--t-title); margin: 2.5rem 0 0.75rem; }
  ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; }
  li + li { margin-top: 0.3rem; }
  dl { display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; gap: 0.35rem 1.5rem; margin: 0; }
  dt { color: var(--muted); }
  dd { margin: 0; }
  .about :global(.side) { position: sticky; top: 2rem; }
  .about :global(.side img), .about :global(img.side) { width: 100%; height: auto; }
  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    .about { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .about :global(.side) { position: static; }
  }
</style>
